# Line-ending policy for the governed index pages. Added 2026-08-31 by R0 of the index
# pattern-book super plan.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Before this file, the two governed index pages in this repo carried
# OPPOSITE working-tree endings: public-index.html was CRLF throughout and
# private-index.html was LF throughout. With core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a
# generator writing LF and a git operation restoring CRLF made the byte count of a governed
# page oscillate by exactly one byte per line with no content change at all, which made every
# byte measurement of these files unreproducible and made --check drift detection unreliable.
#
# WHY LF RATHER THAN CRLF. It is what the repository already stores. Every one of these blobs
# is LF with zero carriage returns at HEAD and at origin/main, because autocrlf=true normalizes
# on the way in. It is also what the generators already emit: build_dev_previews.py and
# build_quick_links.py both open with newline="", and build_pattern_book.py declares a
# "Fixed LF policy (Ultra Plan 1.3)" at its own writer. Declaring CRLF would put this file at
# war with every generator run, which is the oscillation it exists to end.
#
# A generator writing into any file matched here MUST open with newline="" so it emits LF.
# Do not write "preserve whatever ending the file already had": what a generator finds depends
# on whether git or another generator wrote last, which is the instability itself.
*-index.html text eol=lf
